index=main sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"
| rex field=_raw "Name='Image'>(?<Image>[^<]+)"
| rex field=_raw "Name='CommandLine'>(?<CommandLine>[^<]+)"
| search Image="*powershell*" OR CommandLine="*schtasks*"
| table _time Image CommandLine

This Splunk Enterprise query searches Sysmon Operational logs and extracts the process executable name (`Image`) and executed command (`CommandLine`) from raw XML event data. It then 
filters the results to identify suspicious activity involving PowerShell processes or scheduled task commands (`schtasks`), which are commonly associated with attacker persistence and command 
execution techniques. Finally, the query displays the event timestamp, process path, and command line in a clean table format to help analysts investigate potentially malicious behavior.


index=main sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"
| rex field=_raw "Name='CommandLine'>(?<CommandLine>[^<]+)"
| search CommandLine="*schtasks*"
| table _time CommandLine

This Splunk Enterprise query searches Sysmon logs and extracts the executed command-line data from raw XML events. It then filters for commands containing `schtasks`, allowing analysts to 
detect scheduled task activity commonly associated with persistence techniques used by attackers.
